      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 3.64,
          "en": "Now that's it for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.64,
          "end": 5.32,
          "en": "this very thorough introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.32,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "to the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 8.18,
          "en": "We're going to see more of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.18,
          "end": 9.68,
          "en": "throughout the rest of the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 9.68,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "but with this module you should have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 16.31,
          "en": "a first thorough idea of what the Composition API is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.31,
          "end": 19.28,
          "en": "Well, and what is it about, and why do we have it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.28,
          "end": 21.41,
          "en": "First of all, as I emphasized many times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.41,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "throughout the module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 24.68,
          "en": "it's an alternative to the Options API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 24.68,
          "end": 26.92,
          "en": "You don't have to use it if you don't like it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 26.92,
          "end": 29.87,
          "en": "or if it just doesn't make sense for your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 29.87,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "but you can use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 34.31,
          "en": "and then you will use the setup method, which you saw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 34.31,
          "end": 37.72,
          "en": "to expose logic and data to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.72,
          "end": 40.25,
          "en": "and the idea behind the Composition API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.25,
          "end": 42.27,
          "en": "is that it's function based.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 45.14,
          "en": "You have all those functions you import from Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 45.14,
          "end": 48.04,
          "en": "like ref, react, compute, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 48.04,
          "end": 50.16,
          "en": "All used in that setup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.16,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "and that this allows you to keep code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 55.79,
          "en": "that is related logically to gather in one place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.79,
          "end": 58.793,
          "en": "instead of splitting it across multiple options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.75,
          "end": 61.61,
          "en": "Data and reactivity of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.61,
          "end": 64.66,
          "en": "is an important concept in Vue in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 64.66,
          "end": 68.4,
          "en": "and of course, they are found also in the Composition API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.4,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "and here we can manage data as refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 74.97,
          "en": "So as individual values or in object which is in ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.97,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "or we use the reactive function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 79.34,
          "en": "to create reactive objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.34,
          "end": 80.99,
          "en": "I talked about the differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.99,
          "end": 82.58,
          "en": "and how to work with these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.58,
          "end": 85.113,
          "en": "in great depth throughout this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.14,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "Reactivity is a key concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 90.57,
          "en": "and one of the most important takeaways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 94.465,
          "en": "really is that you can create reactive refs or objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 94.465,
          "end": 97.37,
          "en": "but that their nested properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 97.37,
          "end": 99.87,
          "en": "are not necessarily reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 102.743,
          "en": "As I also emphasized throughout this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 104.83,
          "end": 106.93,
          "en": "Now data and reactivity is a key concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 106.93,
          "end": 108.35,
          "en": "but of course, not everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 108.35,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "We also have methods, computed and watchers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113,
          "en": "when using the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 113,
          "end": 114.61,
          "en": "and in the Composition API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 114.61,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "methods become regular functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 118.55,
          "en": "which you define in the setup method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 118.55,
          "end": 120.77,
          "en": "and which you then may expose to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 120.77,
          "end": 123.466,
          "en": "by returning it in that object which you return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 123.466,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "in the setup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 128.77,
          "en": "and then you also have computed properties and watchers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 128.77,
          "end": 132.02,
          "en": "which are defined with these imported functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 132.02,
          "end": 134.123,
          "en": "which you import from the Vue framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 135.43,
          "end": 138.78,
          "en": "Now if we have a closer look at this setup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 138.78,
          "end": 141.34,
          "en": "or setup method which we define in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 141.34,
          "end": 143.652,
          "en": "our component conflict object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 143.652,
          "end": 146.85,
          "en": "this setup function, or this setup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 146.85,
          "end": 150.4,
          "en": "is called by Vue, when the component is created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 150.4,
          "end": 154,
          "en": "and in there you define all the data and logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 154,
          "end": 155.23,
          "en": "for this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 155.23,
          "end": 157.91,
          "en": "and most importantly for the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 157.91,
          "end": 159.66,
          "en": "So what you return in setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 159.66,
          "end": 162.82999999999998,
          "en": "is available in the template as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 162.82999999999998,
          "end": 165.82999999999998,
          "en": "In setup itself all the receives two arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 165.82999999999998,
          "end": 168.46,
          "en": "which are passed and automatically by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 168.46,
          "end": 170.63,
          "en": "when it calls setup for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 170.63,
          "end": 173.72,
          "en": "and that is the reactive props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 173.72,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "with all the props you're getting for this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 180.45,
          "en": "and this context object with the fall through props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 180.45,
          "end": 183.55,
          "en": "those attributes, with slot data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 183.55,
          "end": 185.32,
          "en": "and with this emit function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 185.32,
          "end": 187.933,
          "en": "which you can use for emitting a custom event.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
